> The soul of this dish lies in the harmony of three flavors: the sourness from fermented mustard greens, the heat from Sichuan peppercorns, and the umami from the fish. The key is to not overcook the fish—drop them gently into a gently simmering broth and leave them untouched until they turn firm and opaque.

== Slice and Marinate the Fish ==

Lay @catfish fillets{680%g} on a chopping board. Using a sharp knife, slice at a 45° angle into thin, wide pieces—about 5 mm thick and 5 cm long.

Transfer to a bowl and add:
- @Shaoxing wine{1%tbsp}
- @salt{½%tsp}
- @white pepper{¼%tsp}
- @cornstarch{2%tsp}

Use your hands to gently coat each piece. Set aside to marinate while you prepare the other ingredients.

== Prepare the Vegetables ==

Rinse @pickled mustard greens{200%g} under running water, then soak in fresh water for ~{10-20%minutes} to reduce their saltiness. The time depends on how salty the preserves are—taste a piece. It will mellow once cooked.

Drain and squeeze out all excess water. Cut into 3 cm pieces, slicing the thick stems at an angle for better texture.

== Build the Broth ==

Heat @neutral oil{2%tbsp} in a #wok{} over medium-high heat until shimmering.

Add the aromatics and fry until fragrant, about ~{1%minute}:
- @minced ginger{1%tsp}
- @garlic{5%cloves} (minced, divided)
- @scallions{3%stalks} (sliced, divided)
- @Sichuan pickled chilies{1%tbsp} (optional, chopped)

Push the aromatics to the side and add the @pickled mustard greens{200%g}. Stir-fry for ~{1%minute} to coat them in the oil.

Pour in @water{600%ml}. Bring to a full boil, then reduce to a gentle simmer. Cover and cook for ~{3%minutes} to develop the broth.

== Cook the Fish ==

Gently drop the marinated fish slices into the simmering broth one at a time—do not crowd them. Leave space between each piece for even cooking.

Do not stir. Let the fish simmer undisturbed for ~{2-3%minutes} until they turn opaque and firm. They should curl slightly. Overcooking makes them tough and mealy.

== Sizzle the Toppings ==

Transfer the fish and broth to a large serving bowl.

Scatter the remaining fresh aromatics over the top:
- @garlic{⅓%clove} (minced)
- @scallions{⅓%stalk} (sliced)
- @dried chilies{5} (chopped, to taste)
- @Sichuan peppercorns{1%tsp}
- @toasted sesame seeds{1%tsp}

Heat @neutral oil{2%tbsp} in a small pan until just beginning to smoke. Carefully pour the hot oil directly over the toppings—this sizzle releases all the fragrant oils.

Serve immediately with steamed rice.